{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 64,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.64.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.64.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, a Psalm of David. Hear my voice, O God, in my prayer: preserve my life from fear of the enemy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.64.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.64.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hide me from the secret counsel of the wicked; from the insurrection of the workers of iniquity:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.64.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.64.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who whet their tongue like a sword, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bend ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their bows to shoot",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their arrows, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bitter words:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.64.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.64.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That they may shoot in secret at the perfect: suddenly do they shoot at him, and fear not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.64.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.64.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They encourage themselves ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an evil matter: they commune of laying snares privily; they say, Who will see them?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.64.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.64.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They search out iniquities; they accomplish a diligent search: both the inward ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thought",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of every one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and the heart, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " deep.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.64.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.64.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But God shall shoot at them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an arrow; suddenly shall they be wounded.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.64.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.64.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So they shall make their own tongue to fall upon themselves: all that see them shall flee away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.64.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.64.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all men shall fear, and shall declare the work of God; for they shall wisely consider of his doing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.64.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.64.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The righteous shall be glad in the LORD, and shall trust in him; and all the upright in heart shall glory.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
